{"id":"mahabharata-12-328","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":328,"title":"अष्टाविंशत्यधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 328 · The names of Krishna","summary":{"en":"Janamejaya asks for the meaning of the many names with which Vyasa and his pupils praised Madhusudana. Vaishampayana explains names such as Rudra, the matted, shaven wanderer who lives in cremation grounds, and tells how Fire and Soma, born of one womb, hold up the worlds.","kn":"ವ್ಯಾಸ ಮತ್ತು ಶಿಷ್ಯರು ಮಧುಸೂದನನನ್ನು ಸ್ತುತಿಸಿದ ಅನೇಕ ನಾಮಗಳ ಅರ್ಥ ಹೇಳಲು ಜನಮೇಜಯ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಜಟಾಧಾರಿ, ಮುಂಡ, ಶ್ಮಶಾನವಾಸಿ ರುದ್ರ ಮೊದಲಾದ ಹೆಸರುಗಳನ್ನು ವೈಶಂಪಾಯನ ವಿವರಿಸಿ, ಒಂದೇ ಯೋನಿಯಿಂದ ಹುಟ್ಟಿದ ಅಗ್ನಿ-ಸೋಮ ಲೋಕಗಳನ್ನು ಧರಿಸುವುದನ್ನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"जनमेजय व्यास और शिष्यों द्वारा मधुसूदन की स्तुति में गाए अनेक नामों के अर्थ पूछते हैं। वैशम्पायन रुद्र जैसे नामों की व्याख्या करते हैं और बताते हैं कि एक ही योनि से उपजे अग्नि और सोम लोकों को धारण करते हैं।","te":"వ్యాసుడు, శిష్యులు మధుసూదనుని స్తుతించిన అనేక నామాల అర్థం చెప్పమని జనమేజయుడు అడుగుతాడు. వైశంపాయనుడు జటాధారి, ముండుడు, శ్మశానవాసి రుద్రుడు వంటి పేర్లను వివరించి, ఒకే యోని నుండి పుట్టిన అగ్ని సోములు లోకాలను ధరిస్తారని చెబుతాడు.","ta":"வியாசரும் சீடர்களும் மதுசூதனனைப் புகழ்ந்த பல பெயர்களின் பொருளைக் கூறுமாறு ஜனமேஜயன் கேட்க, சடையன், மொட்டையன், சுடுகாட்டுவாசி ருத்ரன் போன்ற பெயர்களை வைசம்பாயனர் விளக்கி, ஒரே கருவில் பிறந்த அக்னியும் சோமனும் உலகங்களைத் தாங்குவதைக் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"വ്യാസനും ശിഷ്യന്മാരും മധുസൂദനനെ സ്തുതിച്ച അനേകം നാമങ്ങളുടെ അർത്ഥം ജനമേജയൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. ശ്മശാനത്തിൽ വസിക്കുന്ന, ജടയും മൊട്ടത്തലയും ഉള്ള അലഞ്ഞുതിരിയുന്നവനായ രുദ്രൻ എന്ന നാമം തുടങ്ങിയവ വൈശമ്പായനൻ വിശദീകരിക്കുന്നു; ഒരേ ഗർഭത്തിൽ ജനിച്ച അഗ്നിയും സോമനും ലോകങ്ങളെ താങ്ങിനിർത്തുന്നതെങ്ങനെയെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.328; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अस्तौषीद्यैरिमं व्यासः सशिष्यो मधुसूदनम् ।\nनामभिर्विविधैरेषां निरुक्तं भगवन्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blessed one, tell me the meaning of the many names with which Vyasa and his disciples praised Madhusudana."}},{"n":2,"text":"वक्तुमर्हसि शुश्रूषोः प्रजापतिपतेर्हरेः ।\nश्रुत्वा भवेयं यत्पूतः शरच्चन्द्र इवामलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You ought to explain them to me, eager to hear about Hari, lord of the lords of creatures; by hearing it I would become pure, like the spotless autumn moon."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"शृणु राजन्यथाचष्ट फल्गुनस्य हरिर्विभुः ।\nप्रसन्नात्मात्मनो नाम्नां निरुक्तं गुणकर्मजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen, king, to how the all-pervading Hari, with a serene mind, explained to Phalguna the meanings of his names, born of his qualities and deeds."}},{"n":4,"text":"नामभिः कीर्तितैस्तस्य केशवस्य महात्मनः ।\nपृष्टवान्केशवं राजन्फल्गुनः परवीरहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, when the names of the great Keshava had been recited, Arjuna, slayer of enemy heroes, questioned Keshava."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"भगवन्भूतभव्येश सर्वभूतसृगव्यय ।\nलोकधाम जगन्नाथ लोकानामभयप्रद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blessed one, lord of past and future, imperishable creator of all beings, abode of the worlds, lord of the universe, giver of fearlessness to the worlds!"}},{"n":6,"text":"यानि नामानि ते देव कीर्तितानि महर्षिभिः ।\nवेदेषु सपुराणेषु यानि गुह्यानि कर्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O God, I wish to hear from you the meanings of those names of yours that the great sages have sung, in the Vedas and Puranas, and the secret ones that come from your deeds."}},{"n":7,"text":"तेषां निरुक्तं त्वत्तोऽहं श्रोतुमिच्छामि केशव ।\nन ह्यन्यो वर्तयेन्नाम्नां निरुक्तं त्वामृते प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord, no one other than you could expound the meanings of these names."}},{"text":"श्रीभगवानुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Blessed Lord said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"ऋग्वेदे सयजुर्वेदे तथैवाथर्वसामसु ।\nपुराणे सोपनिषदे तथैव ज्योतिषेऽर्जुन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, in the Rig Veda with the Yajur, and likewise in the Atharva and Sama Vedas, in the Purana with the Upanishads, and in astronomy too,"}},{"n":9,"text":"सांख्ये च योगशास्त्रे च आयुर्वेदे तथैव च ।\nबहूनि मम नामानि कीर्तितानि महर्षिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and in Samkhya, in the science of yoga, and in the science of medicine, the great sages have sung many names of mine."}},{"n":10,"text":"गौणानि तत्र नामानि कर्मजानि च कानिचित् ।\nनिरुक्तं कर्मजानां च शृणुष्व प्रयतोऽनघ ।\nकथ्यमानं मया तात त्वं हि मेऽर्धं स्मृतः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some of those names are qualitative and some arise from deeds. Listen attentively, sinless one, to the explanation of those born of deeds, as I tell it, dear friend, for you were long ago declared my other half."}},{"n":11,"text":"नमोऽतियशसे तस्मै देहिनां परमात्मने ।\nनारायणाय विश्वाय निर्गुणाय गुणात्मने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Homage to him of great fame, the supreme self of embodied beings, Narayana, the universal one, free of the qualities yet the soul of the qualities."}},{"n":12,"text":"यस्य प्रसादजो ब्रह्मा रुद्रश्च क्रोधसंभवः ।\nयोऽसौ योनिर्हि सर्वस्य स्थावरस्य चरस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"From his grace Brahma is born, and Rudra from his wrath; he is the source of everything, moving and unmoving."}},{"n":13,"text":"अष्टादशगुणं यत्तत्सत्त्वं सत्त्ववतां वर ।\nप्रकृतिः सा परा मह्यं रोदसी योगधारिणी ।\nऋता सत्यामराजय्या लोकानामात्मसंज्ञिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the virtuous, that goodness which has eighteen qualities is my supreme nature, which upholds heaven and earth by yoga; it is order and truth, unconquerable by gods, and is known as the self of the worlds."}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्मात्सर्वाः प्रवर्तन्ते सर्गप्रलयविक्रियाः ।\nततो यज्ञश्च यष्टा च पुराणः पुरुषो विराट् ।\nअनिरुद्ध इति प्रोक्तो लोकानां प्रभवाप्ययः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From it proceed all the changes of creation and dissolution; from it come sacrifice, the sacrificer, and the ancient cosmic Person, called Aniruddha, the origin and end of the worlds."}},{"n":15,"text":"ब्राह्मे रात्रिक्षये प्राप्ते तस्य ह्यमिततेजसः ।\nप्रसादात्प्रादुरभवत्पद्मं पद्मनिभेक्षण ।\nतत्र ब्रह्मा समभवत्स तस्यैव प्रसादजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lotus-eyed one, when the night of Brahma came to its close, a lotus arose by the grace of that boundless splendor, and from it Brahma was born, a child of his grace."}},{"n":16,"text":"अह्नः क्षये ललाटाच्च सुतो देवस्य वै तथा ।\nक्रोधाविष्टस्य संजज्ञे रुद्रः संहारकारकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of the day, from the forehead of the god, who was seized by anger, a son was born, Rudra, the destroyer."}},{"n":17,"text":"एतौ द्वौ विबुधश्रेष्ठौ प्रसादक्रोधजौ स्मृतौ ।\nतदादेशितपन्थानौ सृष्टिसंहारकारकौ ।\nनिमित्तमात्रं तावत्र सर्वप्राणिवरप्रदौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two best of gods are remembered as born of grace and wrath; they follow paths he ordained, doing creation and destruction, mere instruments, granting boons to all beings."}},{"n":18,"text":"कपर्दी जटिलो मुण्डः श्मशानगृहसेवकः ।\nउग्रव्रतधरो रुद्रो योगी त्रिपुरदारुणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rudra, with matted hair and shaved head, who frequents the cremation ground, observes fierce vows, is a yogi and terrible to the Tripuras,"}},{"n":19,"text":"दक्षक्रतुहरश्चैव भगनेत्रहरस्तथा ।\nनारायणात्मको ज्ञेयः पाण्डवेय युगे युगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"and who destroyed Daksha's sacrifice and Bhaga's eyes, should be known, son of Pandu, as having Narayana for his self, age after age."}},{"n":20,"text":"तस्मिन्हि पूज्यमाने वै देवदेवे महेश्वरे ।\nसंपूजितो भवेत्पार्थ देवो नारायणः प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Maheshvara, the god of gods, is worshipped, Son of Pritha, the lord God Narayana is worshipped too."}},{"n":21,"text":"अहमात्मा हि लोकानां विश्वानां पाण्डुनन्दन ।\nतस्मादात्मानमेवाग्रे रुद्रं संपूजयाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am the self of all the worlds, son of Pandu, and so I first worship my own self, Rudra."}},{"n":22,"text":"यद्यहं नार्चयेयं वै ईशानं वरदं शिवम् ।\nआत्मानं नार्चयेत्कश्चिदिति मे भावितं मनः ।\nमया प्रमाणं हि कृतं लोकः समनुवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"My mind reasoned that if I did not worship the boon-giving, auspicious Ishana, no one would worship the Self; and the world follows the standard I set."}},{"n":23,"text":"प्रमाणानि हि पूज्यानि ततस्तं पूजयाम्यहम् ।\nयस्तं वेत्ति स मां वेत्ति योऽनु तं स हि मामनु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Standards deserve to be honored, and therefore I worship him. Whoever knows him knows me, and whoever follows him follows me."}},{"n":24,"text":"रुद्रो नारायणश्चैव सत्त्वमेकं द्विधाकृतम् ।\nलोके चरति कौन्तेय व्यक्तिस्थं सर्वकर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rudra and Narayana are one essence made two, moving in the world, abiding in manifest form in all actions, son of Kunti."}},{"n":25,"text":"न हि मे केनचिद्देयो वरः पाण्डवनन्दन ।\nइति संचिन्त्य मनसा पुराणं विश्वमीश्वरम् ।\nपुत्रार्थमाराधितवानात्मानमहमात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Descendant of Pandu, no one can grant me a boon; thinking thus, I worshipped the ancient lord of the universe, my own self, by myself, for the sake of a son."}},{"n":26,"text":"न हि विष्णुः प्रणमति कस्मैचिद्विबुधाय तु ।\nऋत आत्मानमेवेति ततो रुद्रं भजाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vishnu bows to no god apart from the Self; therefore I worship Rudra."}},{"n":27,"text":"सब्रह्मकाः सरुद्राश्च सेन्द्रा देवाः सहर्षिभिः ।\nअर्चयन्ति सुरश्रेष्ठं देवं नारायणं हरिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods with Brahma, Rudra, and Indra, together with the sages, worship the best of gods, Lord Narayana Hari."}},{"n":28,"text":"भविष्यतां वर्ततां च भूतानां चैव भारत ।\nसर्वेषामग्रणीर्विष्णुः सेव्यः पूज्यश्च नित्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Descendant of Bharata, Vishnu is the foremost of all beings, future, present, and past; he is to be served and worshipped always."}},{"n":29,"text":"नमस्व हव्यदं विष्णुं तथा शरणदं नम ।\nवरदं नमस्व कौन्तेय हव्यकव्यभुजं नम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bow to Vishnu, the giver of offerings; bow to him who gives refuge; bow to the giver of boons; bow to the enjoyer of offerings to gods and ancestors."}},{"n":30,"text":"चतुर्विधा मम जना भक्ता एवं हि ते श्रुतम् ।\nतेषामेकान्तिनः श्रेष्ठास्ते चैवानन्यदेवताः ।\nअहमेव गतिस्तेषां निराशीःकर्मकारिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"My devotees are of four kinds, as you have heard. Of them the single-minded, who have no other deity, are best; I alone am the goal of those who act without desire for reward."}},{"n":31,"text":"ये च शिष्टास्त्रयो भक्ताः फलकामा हि ते मताः ।\nसर्वे च्यवनधर्माणः प्रतिबुद्धस्तु श्रेष्ठभाक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The other three kinds of devotees are considered to desire fruits; all of them are subject to falling, but the awakened one gets the best share."}},{"n":32,"text":"ब्रह्माणं शितिकण्ठं च याश्चान्या देवताः स्मृताः ।\nप्रबुद्धवर्याः सेवन्ते मामेवैष्यन्ति यत्परम् ।\nभक्तं प्रति विशेषस्ते एष पार्थानुकीर्तितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The best of the awakened worship Brahma, the blue-throated Shiva, and whatever other deities are remembered, and will reach me, the supreme goal. This, son of Pritha, is how the devotee's distinction was told to you."}},{"n":33,"text":"त्वं चैवाहं च कौन्तेय नरनारायणौ स्मृतौ ।\nभारावतरणार्थं हि प्रविष्टौ मानुषीं तनुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You and I, son of Kunti, are remembered as Nara and Narayana; we have entered human bodies to lighten the earth's burden."}},{"n":34,"text":"जानाम्यध्यात्मयोगांश्च योऽहं यस्माच्च भारत ।\nनिवृत्तिलक्षणो धर्मस्तथाभ्युदयिकोऽपि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know the yogas of the spirit, who I am, and why, Bharata, and I know the dharma marked by withdrawal and the dharma of worldly prosperity."}},{"n":35,"text":"नराणामयनं ख्यातमहमेकः सनातनः ।\nआपो नारा इति प्रोक्ता आपो वै नरसूनवः ।\nअयनं मम तत्पूर्वमतो नारायणो ह्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I alone, the eternal one, am called the resort of men. The waters are called nara, for the waters are the offspring of man; that was my first resting place, so I am Narayana."}},{"n":36,"text":"छादयामि जगद्विश्वं भूत्वा सूर्य इवांशुभिः ।\nसर्वभूताधिवासश्च वासुदेवस्ततो ह्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Becoming like the sun with its rays, I cover the whole universe; and because I dwell in all beings, I am Vasudeva."}},{"n":37,"text":"गतिश्च सर्वभूतानां प्रजानां चापि भारत ।\nव्याप्ता मे रोदसी पार्थ कान्तिश्चाभ्यधिका मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, I am the goal of all beings and creatures; I pervade heaven and earth, son of Pritha, and my radiance is the greater."}},{"n":38,"text":"अधिभूतानि चान्तेऽहं तदिच्छंश्चास्मि भारत ।\nक्रमणाच्चाप्यहं पार्थ विष्णुरित्यभिसंज्ञितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end I am the overlord of beings, and I am the one who wills it, Bharata; and from striding, Partha, I am named Vishnu."}},{"n":39,"text":"दमात्सिद्धिं परीप्सन्तो मां जनाः कामयन्ति हि ।\nदिवं चोर्वीं च मध्यं च तस्माद्दामोदरो ह्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"People seeking success through self-control desire me, in heaven, on earth, and the middle region; therefore I am Damodara."}},{"n":40,"text":"पृश्निरित्युच्यते चान्नं वेदा आपोऽमृतं तथा ।\nममैतानि सदा गर्भे पृश्निगर्भस्ततो ह्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prishni is the name for food, the Vedas, the waters, and the nectar; I always hold these in my womb, so I am Prishnigarbha."}},{"n":41,"text":"ऋषयः प्राहुरेवं मां त्रितकूपाभिपातितम् ।\nपृश्निगर्भ त्रितं पाहीत्येकतद्वितपातितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sages called me thus when I was cast into the well by Trita: \"Prishnigarbha, protect Trita!\", said when Ekata and Dvita had thrown him in."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततः स ब्रह्मणः पुत्र आद्यो ऋषिवरस्त्रितः ।\nउत्ततारोदपानाद्वै पृश्निगर्भानुकीर्तनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Trita, the first of the sages and a son of Brahma, climbed out of the well by reciting the name Prishnigarbha."}},{"n":43,"text":"सूर्यस्य तपतो लोकानग्नेः सोमस्य चाप्युत ।\nअंशवो ये प्रकाशन्ते मम ते केशसंज्ञिताः ।\nसर्वज्ञाः केशवं तस्मान्मामाहुर्द्विजसत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rays of the blazing sun, of fire, and of the moon, which illuminate the worlds, are called my hair; therefore those who know all call me Keshava, best of the twice-born."}},{"n":44,"text":"स्वपत्न्यामाहितो गर्भ उतथ्येन महात्मना ।\nउतथ्येऽन्तर्हिते चैव कदाचिद्देवमायया ।\nबृहस्पतिरथाविन्दत्तां पत्नीं तस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great Utathya had placed a child in the womb of his wife; when Utathya had vanished, once, through the god's illusion, Brihaspati took his wife, Bharata."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततो वै तमृषिश्रेष्ठं मैथुनोपगतं तथा ।\nउवाच गर्भः कौन्तेय पञ्चभूतसमन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, son of Kunti, the child in the womb, formed of the five elements, spoke to that best of sages as he approached her."}},{"n":46,"text":"पूर्वागतोऽहं वरद नार्हस्यम्बां प्रबाधितुम् ।\nएतद्बृहस्पतिः श्रुत्वा चुक्रोध च शशाप च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Giver of boons, I came first; you should not trouble my mother.\" Hearing this, Brihaspati grew angry and cursed him."}},{"n":47,"text":"मैथुनोपगतो यस्मात्त्वयाहं विनिवारितः ।\nतस्मादन्धो जास्यसि त्वं मच्छापान्नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Since you stopped me as I was approaching her, you will be born blind through my curse, no doubt.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"स शापादृषिमुख्यस्य दीर्घं तम उपेयिवान् ।\nस हि दीर्घतमा नाम नाम्ना ह्यासीदृषिः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the curse of that chief of sages he fell into long darkness; he was the sage named Dirghatamas in earlier times."}},{"n":49,"text":"वेदानवाप्य चतुरः साङ्गोपाङ्गान्सनातनान् ।\nप्रयोजयामास तदा नाम गुह्यमिदं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having learned the four eternal Vedas with their limbs and subsidiary parts, he then used this secret name of mine,"}},{"n":50,"text":"आनुपूर्व्येण विधिना केशवेति पुनः पुनः ।\nस चक्षुष्मान्समभवद्गौतमश्चाभवत्पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"repeating \"Keshava\" again and again in due order and rite. He gained sight and became a Gautama once more."}},{"n":51,"text":"एवं हि वरदं नाम केशवेति ममार्जुन ।\nदेवानामथ सर्वेषामृषीणां च महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, Arjuna, my name Keshava is a boon-giving name, for all the gods and the great sages."}},{"n":52,"text":"अग्निः सोमेन संयुक्त एकयोनि मुखं कृतम् ।\nअग्नीषोमात्मकं तस्माज्जगत्कृत्स्नं चराचरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Agni joined with Soma has been made a single-wombed mouth; therefore the whole world, moving and unmoving, is of the nature of Agni and Soma."}},{"n":53,"text":"अपि हि पुराणे भवति ।\nएकयोन्यात्मकावग्नीषोमौ ।\nदेवाश्चाग्निमुखा इति ।\nएकयोनित्वाच्च परस्परं महयन्तो लोकान्धारयत इति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Purana also says this: Agni and Soma have one womb as their nature; the gods have Agni as their mouth; and because of their single origin they honor each other and sustain the worlds."}}]}]}